        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Gatwick Airport, Heathrow Airport, Coldwaltham, Central London, Crawley, London, south-east England, United Kingdom\n- Products: IATA airport codes, ICAO airport codes\n- Topics: airport location, passenger traffic, travel distance\n\nFacts:\n- Gatwick Airport, also known as London Gatwick, has the IATA code LGW and the ICAO code EGKK.\n- Gatwick Airport is a major international airport in south-east England, 29.5 miles south of Central London and 2.7 nautical miles north of Crawley.\n- Gatwick Airport is the second-busiest airport in the United Kingdom by total passenger traffic after London Heathrow.\n- Heathrow Airport, also known as London Heathrow, has the IATA code LHR and the ICAO code EGLL.\n- Heathrow Airport is a major international airport in London, United Kingdom.\n- Coldwaltham is around a 30-minute drive from Gatwick Airport.",
